Problem: Maximum Number of Vowels in a Substring of Given Length (LC 1456)

Pattern: Fixed Size Sliding Window

Approach:

Create a helper function isVowel() to check whether a character is a vowel.
Count the vowels in the first window of size k.
Store the count in maxVowels.
Slide the window one character at a time:
If the outgoing character (s[i-k]) is a vowel, decrement vowelCount.
If the incoming character (s[i]) is a vowel, increment vowelCount.
Update maxVowels.
Return maxVowels.

Time Complexity: O(n)

Space Complexity: O(1)
